ul atomic RMW, its read component obtains the immediately preceding modification of its atomic location in `mo`, under the chosen coherence model; a failed comparison observes a value via a read-only event and contributes no modification to `mo`. The first successful `acquire` must therefore be able to read (`rf`) the initializing `newMutex` write, which is explicitly included in `mo`. An ordinary exclusive write under C42 also occupies its appropriate `mo` position and must be `hb`-ordered as required by the applicable safe-access contract.\n\nA well-formed graph must satisfy explicit typing, source-existence, range-identity, and coherence obligations on `rf` and `mo`. **Specifying `rf` and `mo` alone is insufficient to define a full permitted execution.** The fragment requires a named `EventConsistent` predicate (or equivalent) whose established conjuncts are listed in the corresponding proof statement. No unspecified or inconsistent graph may be accepted merely by postulating a convenient `rf` edge.\n\n## C32. Synchronizes-With — `sw`\n\nThe following are **candidate reference** sources of synchronization:\n\n1. **Atomic protocol:** a release-capable write/RMW (including a `seq_cst` store or RMW) and an acquire-capable read/RMW (including a `seq_cst` load or RMW) on the same atomic unit may establish `sw` when the acquire reads the release through the applicable `rf` relationship and the relevant memory orders provide release/acquire semantics. **Address identity alone is insufficient.** The initial Lean fragment uses **direct `rf`** only; release-sequence-mediated synchronization awaits explicit modeling.\n2. **Context creation:** the parent's `spawn(c)` event `sw`-precedes the child's `start(c)` event, with all prior parent events and subsequent child events related through `po`.\n3. **Completion observation:** `complete(c)` of the terminated context `sw`-precedes a successful `join(c)`, with the completing context's preceding events ordered before `complete(c)` and the joining context's subsequent events ordered after `join(c)`.\n\nA pure `release` (O3), `derive`, `endUse`, or other authority marker **does not itself create `sw`**. A bare `spawn` in the abstract interleaving does not order parent operations executed **after** that `spawn` before the child's later operations. A `join(c)` orders only the events of the context whose completion it actually observes, subject to already established transitive edges; it does not implicitly join live descendants or unrelated contexts.\n\nAdditional synchronization mechanisms are admissible only under an explicit contract with a proof that their event edges have the claimed semantics.\n\n## C33. Happens-Before and Data Races","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"4ca81fe0-2905-483a-8f74-8bba88a49196","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/spec2-m4","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4d326c24-ed4a-42c3-92a4-bccc161d1dc9","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"formal/spec2-m4","slug":"replicated-napping-garden"}
